# firehose-detection settings. Secrets are read from the environment (not
# flags) so they don't show up in `ps`.
#
#   cp env.example .env        # .env is gitignored
#   $EDITOR .env
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#   ./firehose-detection -rules rules.yaml -cursor state.cursor
#
# On startup you should see:
#   msg="bluesky reporting enabled" handle=...
#   msg="discord output enabled" channel=...
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONNECTING TO DISCORD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Create the bot
#    - Go to https://discord.com/developers/applications > New Application.
#    - Open the "Bot" tab > Reset Token > copy it into DISCORD_TOKEN below.
#      (Discord only shows it once. If it leaks, reset it here.)
#    - Leave all three "Privileged Gateway Intents" OFF. None are needed.
#    - On the "General Information" tab, leave "Interactions Endpoint URL"
#      EMPTY. If it is set, Discord sends button clicks to that URL instead
#      of to this bot, and the Report/Dismiss buttons will do nothing.
#
# 2. Invite it to your server
#    - Copy the "Application ID" from "General Information" and open:
#        https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=APPLICATION_ID&scope=bot&permissions=19456
#      19456 = View Channels + Send Messages + Embed Links, which is all it
#      needs. (Or build the same link under OAuth2 > URL Generator: scope
#      "bot", then those three permissions.)
#    - Pick your server and authorize.
#    - If the target channel is private, also add the bot to it:
#      channel settings > Permissions > Add members or roles > the bot.
#
# 3. Get the IDs
#    - Discord: User Settings > Advanced > turn on Developer Mode.
#    - Right-click the channel > Copy Channel ID  -> DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID
#    - (Optional) Server Settings > Roles > right-click your moderator role
#      > Copy Role ID -> DISCORD_REPORT_ROLE_ID. Without it, anyone who can
#      see the channel can press Report.
#
# 4. Report buttons and auto_report rules need a Bluesky account
#    - Log in as the account reports should come from, then go to
#      Settings > Privacy and security > App passwords > Add App Password.
#      Leave "Allow access to your direct messages" unchecked.
#    - Never use the account's main password here.
#    - Without these, matches still post to Discord, just with no buttons,
#      and the process refuses to start if any rule sets auto_report.
#
# Troubleshooting
#    - "discord connect: ... 4004" / "Authentication failed": wrong token
#      (copy the Bot token, not the Client Secret or Public Key).
#    - "send failed ... 50001 Missing Access": the bot can't see the channel;
#      see the private-channel step above.
#    - "send failed ... 50013 Missing Permissions": the bot lacks Send
#      Messages or Embed Links in that channel.
#    - Buttons show "This interaction failed": an Interactions Endpoint URL is
#      set (step 1), or the process isn't running.

# --- Discord (output is enabled when DISCORD_TOKEN is set) -------------------
DISCORD_TOKEN=
DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=
DISCORD_REPORT_ROLE_ID=

# --- Bluesky (needed for the Report button and auto_report rules) -----------
BSKY_HANDLE=yourmodaccount.bsky.social
BSKY_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
# Where to log in. Leave as-is unless the account is on a self-hosted PDS.
BSKY_PDS=https://bsky.social
